       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 2550 mg three times daily comes to 7,650 mg/day, which is three times the maximum recommended metformin dose of 2,550 mg/day. That's a dangerous dose with a real risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nI suspect 2,550 mg was meant as the total daily dose. If so, the order would be **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals**.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day), or\n- A different dose. Many clinicians start lower, for example 500 mg BID or 500 mg TID, and titrate up.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away."
